<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4384" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">attrectātĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adt-</span></b> ), ōnis,
			f.
		attrecto. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A touching</i>, <i>handling</i>
			(post-Aug.), <i><span class="en">Gell. 11, 18, 23</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">boves frequenti manūs attrectatione
					mansuescere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. Mart. 12, 1 al.</span></i>
			— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			gram., <i>a term applied to words which denote a taking
				of many things together;</i> as, fasceatim, <i><span class="en">Quint. 1,
				4, 20</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
